                    <div class="benefits-slide">
                        <article class="benefit-card"><span class="benefit-icon" aria-hidden="true">£</span><h3>Mediating Saves Money</h3><p>Mediating, rather than litigating allows you to keep your hard earned money. Don’t waste it on expensive solicitors, court &amp; experts.</p><p>Think of all the money you can save, think of what else you could spend it on. Pay off your mortgage, buy the kids a house, pay for their education, weddings. Go on that overdue holiday, buy that new car? Don’t waste your hard earned money and savings on litigation.</p></article>
                        <article class="benefit-card"><span class="benefit-icon" aria-hidden="true">◷</span><h3>Mediating Saves Time</h3><p>We can mediate for you within 14 days of contact. In person or online via Zoom. We can end your dispute in 4-8 hours.</p><p>It will not take the months or even years that court and tribunal actions take! Think of all that precious time, that you can spend doing the things you enjoy, with those you love the most.</p></article>
                        <article class="benefit-card"><span class="benefit-icon" aria-hidden="true">♥</span><h3>Mediating Ends Worry</h3><p>No more headache, physical, emotional &amp; mental pain. No more stress, sleepless nights, no more time off work, &amp; no more uncertainty!</p><p>Finally peace of mind, imagine how that would feel? Life is way too short, improving your mental and physical health now.</p></article>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefits-slide">
                        <article class="benefit-card"><span class="benefit-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span><h3>Convenience Of Mediating</h3><p>Our mediators cover the whole of the UK and will travel to you. With no charge for travel time or costs. If you have an international dispute, travel costs (flights, hotels) are charged at cost.</p></article>
                        <article class="benefit-card"><span class="benefit-icon" aria-hidden="true">♙</span><h3>Mediation Is Confidential</h3><p>Totally confidential and without prejudice. Therefore no one who attends the mediation can discuss what happened there with any outside persons. To include a judge if the dispute progresses down the court route.</p></article>
                        <article class="benefit-card"><span class="benefit-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚖</span><h3>Mediating v Court</h3><p>Totally confidential and without prejudice. Therefore no one who attends the mediation can discuss what happened there with any outside persons. To include a judge if the dispute progresses down the court route.</p></article>
                    </div>
